    "lawCode": "Amd §1285-u, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6317\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to the septic system replacement fund\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make it easier for homeowners to access\nfunding available in the Septic System Replacement Fund.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill amends section 1285-u of the public authorities law to\nauthorize septic system installers, upon written agreement from\nhomeowners, to receive direct reimbursement from the Septic System\nReplacement Fund.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe 2017-18 State Budget authorized the creation of a Septic System\nReplacement Fund in order to incentivize the replacement of failing\nseptic systems and the installation of more effective septic systems,\nsuch as advanced nitrogen removal systems.  The Fund provides\nreimbursement to homeowners eligible to participate in the program.\nConcerns have been expressed about the out-of-pocket expenses that\ncould be incurred by homeowners. This bill would allow septic\ncontractors, upon receipt of written authorization from eligible\nhomeowners, to receive reimbursement directly. Such direct\nreimbursement would help maximize participation and ensure that\nlow-income homeowners can also afford to participate.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nsection 9 of part T of the laws of 2017, takes effect.\n",
